# One input per line. A blank line and a `#` line are skipped, and `~` on its
# own is the empty string, which no other notation here can write.

# --- what this repository, its bundle and its package already write ---------
shelves.decisions.path
identifier_schemes.decision_id.pattern
vocabularies.lifecycle_state
kinds.design_spec.identifier
kinds.decision_register.language
regimes.language.ste_house
regimes.voice.narrative
relations.forbids
shelves.playbooks
kinds.playbook

# --- the shapes the grammar admits and nothing has written yet --------------
# One segment is an address. It names a whole declaration, and `remove:` is
# where that is useful.
shelves
# Digits and `_` are segment characters, and case is kept.
kinds.adr_2
kinds.ADR
# A list index parses, and this is where the grammar stops. `0` is a legal key
# name, so no lexical rule can tell an index from a key. The refusal is the
# resolver's, on the node the address lands on: an address that reaches into a
# list is an error, because a list position is not stable across an upstream
# release, and `add_to` and `remove_from` are what a list takes instead.
regimes.lifecycle.standard.transitions.0

# --- what the grammar refuses -----------------------------------------------
~
.kinds
kinds.
kinds..playbook
# A hyphen is refused today. Nothing in the language needs one, and Q2 settles
# the direction to guess in: relaxing a rule later is free, and adding one later
# is a finding against every source that already used the form.
kinds.play-book
kinds.play book
# A reference is not an address.
$vocabularies.lifecycle_state
